## Step 2 — the defect and the fix
`TestMergeDriverWithLockedConfig_E2E/handles_read-only_git_config_file` fails on
this host today, before any of this item's changes. The manager already
reproduced the cause in isolation with git 2.43.0: `git config` writes through a
lock file plus a rename inside `.git/`, so a mode-0444 `.git/config` is still
rewritten as long as the `.git/` DIRECTORY is writable. The test chmods the file
but not the directory, so its premise is false, `MergeDriver` correctly returns
nil, and the assertion "expected error when git config is read-only" fires.

The product code is right; the test is wrong. Fix the test so it actually locks
the config against writes — make `.git/` itself non-writable for the duration —
and restore permissions in the existing `defer` so the test's own cleanup still
works (a test that leaves an unwritable directory behind breaks `t.TempDir`
cleanup and every later run). Keep the assertion that `MergeDriver` returns an
error mentioning "failed to update git merge driver config". Do not delete the
test, do not `t.Skip` it, and do not add it to `.test-skip`.

Verify your fix actually tests something: with your change in place the test must
FAIL if you temporarily make `MergeDriver` return nil unconditionally. Check that
by hand, revert the temporary edit, and say in the build report that you did.

